theory.intro:
A circle with centre $(a,b)$ and radius $r$ has equation $(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}=r^{2}$ — the circle $x^{2}+y^{2}=r^{2}$ translated $a$ across and $b$ up. **Complete the square** to reach this form from the **expanded form** $x^{2}+y^{2}+Dx+Ey+F=0$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\draw[<->] (-2.6,0) -- (6.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-2.6) -- (0,6.8) node[above] {$y$};
\coordinate (C) at (2,2);
\coordinate (P) at (4.828,4.828);
\coordinate (Q) at (4.828,2);
\draw[thick,blue] (C) circle (4);
\draw (C) -- (P) node[pos=0.62, above left] {$r$};
\draw (C) -- (Q) node[midway, below] {$x-a$};
\draw (Q) -- (P) node[pos=0.35, left] {$y-b$};
\coordinate (qa) at ($(Q)!0.4cm!(C)$);
\coordinate (qb) at ($(Q)!0.4cm!(P)$);
\draw (qa) -- ($(qa)+(qb)-(Q)$) -- (qb);
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (C) {$(a,b)$};
\fill (P) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above right] at (P) {$(x,y)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
Sketch the circle $(x-1)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4$, showing the centre.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw[<->] (-4,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-5)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.solution_text:
$(x-1)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4$
Centre $(1,-2)$ and radius $2$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw[<->] (-4,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-5)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\coordinate (C) at (1,-2);
\draw[thick,blue] (C) circle (2);
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt);
\node[right] at (C) {$(1,-2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
The circle shown has its centre and radius marked.
Determine its equation.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.55]
\draw[<->] (-6,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3)--(0,5) node[above] {$y$};
\coordinate (C) at (-2,1);
\draw[thick,blue] (C) circle (3);
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below] at (C) {$(-2,1)$};
\draw[dashed] (C) -- (1,1) node[midway, above] {$3$};
